# JSONPlaceholder API Test Suite

## Overview

This project contains pytest API tests for the JSONPlaceholder posts, comments, and users resources. Tests run automatically on every push via GitHub Actions.

- API: [JSONPlaceholder](https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com)
- Stack: Python, pytest, and the Requests library

## Setup

Create and activate a virtual environment from the project root:

```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

Install the dependencies:

```powershell
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Run

Run the test suite:

```powershell
pytest -v
```

## Coverage

| Endpoint | Method | What is checked |
|---|---|---|
| `/posts` | GET | Returns 100 posts with the expected fields and types |
| `/posts/{id}` | GET | Valid post returns `200`; nonexistent IDs return `404` and `{}` |
| `/posts?userId={id}` | GET | Every result belongs to the requested user; unknown users return `[]` |
| `/posts` | POST | Returns `201`, echoes the submitted fields, and includes an integer ID |
| `/posts/{id}` | PUT | Returns `200` and replaces the post with the submitted fields |
| `/posts/{id}` | PATCH | Returns `200` and changes only the requested field |
| `/posts/{id}` | DELETE | Returns `200` and an empty object |
| `/posts/{id}/comments` | GET | Returns comments for the requested post |
| `/comments?postId={id}` | GET | Returns the same comments as the nested comments route |
| `/users` | GET | Confirms every post's `userId` belongs to a real user |

## Known limitations

- JSONPlaceholder fakes write operations; created posts are not saved, so the retrieval test for a created post is marked with `xfail`.
- JSONPlaceholder does not validate input for the write endpoints.
- Tests depend on JSONPlaceholder's fixed seed data. For example, user `5` owns posts `41-50`, and only IDs `1-100` are defined for posts.


